\"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"a\", \"c\", \"c\", \"e\", \"s\", \"s\", \".\", \"r\", \"e\", \"d\", \"h\", \"a\", \"t\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"e\", \"r\", \"r\", \"a\", \"t\", \"a\", \"/\", \"R\", \"H\", \"S\", \"A\", \"-\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \":\", \"5\", \"6\", \"5\", \"2\", \"4\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"a\", \"c\", \"c\", \"e\", \"s\", \"s\", \".\", \"r\", \"e\", \"d\", \"h\", \"a\", \"t\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"s\", \"e\", \"c\", \"u\", \"r\", \"i\", \"t\", \"y\", \"/\", \"c\", \"v\", \"e\", \"/\", \"C\", \"V\", \"E\", \"-\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \"-\", \"1\", \"8\", \"9\", \"6\", \"3\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"b\", \"u\", \"g\", \"z\", \"i\", \"l\", \"l\", \"a\", \".\", \"r\", \"e\", \"d\", \"h\", \"a\", \"t\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"s\", \"h\", \"o\", \"w\", \"_\", \"b\", \"u\", \"g\", \".\", \"c\", \"g\", \"i\", \"?\", \"i\", \"d\", \"=\", \"2\", \"5\", \"1\", \"1\", \"5\", \"9\", \"5\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n            ## 以下内容是基于此漏洞的搜索结果:\n                [webpage 0 begin] [title] GitHub - kyos-public/keycloak-cve-2026-18963-hunt: Hunt for CVE-2026 ...\n [description] The vulnerability CVE-2026-18963 is a flaw in the reset-credentials flow of keycloak-services (keycloak#51833). An unauthenticated attacker can complete the password reset process for any user without clicking the mail verification link, then set a new password on the account. No user interaction is required.\n [link] https://github.com/kyos-public/keycloak-cve-2026-18963-hunt\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] CVE-2026-18963 : Authorization Flaw in Keycloak Services by Red Hat\n [description] Uncover the vulnerability in Keycloak Services, where attackers can reset user passwords without verification. Learn about CVE-2026-18963.\n [link] https://securityvulnerability.io/vulnerability/CVE-2026-18963\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] CVE-2026-18963 - Exploits & Severity - Feedly\n [description] Red Hat and the Keycloak project have released security updates for CVE-2026-18963, a critical vulnerability that could allow an unauthenticated remote attacker to reset the password of another user and potentially take control of arbitrary accounts, including administrative accounts. Under vulnerable conditions, a specially crafted request can interfere with the reset-credentials ...\n [link] https://feedly.com/cve/CVE-2026-18963\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2026-18963 | Critical | CVETodo\n [description] CVE-2026-18963 is a CVSS 9.1 critical-severity vulnerability in Red Hat products. See exploitation status, patch guidance, and technical details.\n [link] https://cvetodo.com/cve/CVE-2026-18963\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] CVE-2026-18963 - Keycloak-services: keycloak-services: unauthenticated ...\n [description] Aug. 18, 2026, 5:16 p.m. Last Modified : Aug. 20, 2026, 2:17 p.m. Remotely Exploit : Yes ! Source : [email protected] Impact Affected Products The following products are affected by CVE-2026-18963 vulnerability. Even if cvefeed.io is aware of the exact versions of the products that are affected, the information is not represented in the table ...\n [link] https://cvefeed.io/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-18963\n [webpage 4 end]\n[webpage 5 begin] [title] GitHub - SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs: A community-curated, verified collection of Proof-of-Concept exploits for CVEs disclosed in 2026. · GitHub\n [description] A community-curated, verified collection of Proof-of-Concept exploits for CVEs disclosed in 2026. - SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs\n [link] https://github.com/SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs\n [webpage 5 end]\n[webpage 6 begin] [title] CVE-2026-18963 - Red Hat Customer Portal\n [description] The Red Hat Product Security team has assessed the severity of this vulnerability as Critical, given that it can be exploited by an unauthenticated remote